1. `Note:` when you are performing any algorithm on a selected part of a string or any 
    container or anything like substring , sorting , reversing a string then make sure 
    to use `if(a>b) swap(a,b);`  this will make sure our starting part of a algorithm that 
    is `a` is always less than b.
    
    
2. `Basics of command line interface (CLI)` : 
	1. `Opening terminal ` : `ctrl+alt+t`
	2. `Copy paste shortcut keys` : `ctrl+shift+c` for copy and `ctrl+shift+v` for paste 
	    on command line
	3. `auto completion` : type name of external program , file name or builtin command 
	    partial and then press tab if there is only one possibility for that then this 
	    will autocomplete otherwise double pressing tab will list (including previous tab)
        will list all possibilities for that partial typing . 
	4. `opening vs code through terminal in linux` : open terminal and type `code` this 
	    will open vs code `code 20-10-2026` this will open vs code with particular file 
	    that is `20-10-2026`.  And opening particular folder from desktop then `cd ~/Downloads /19-10-2026 & code`
	    this will launch `19-10-2026` folder in vs code. (means we opening that folder in 
	    our vs code by this one command only). 
